{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.72,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J12", "U5"],
      "pins": ["J12.A4", "U5.2", "U5.1"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "VBUS"],
      "observed": "On mcu.kicad_sch (page 3, top-right) the USB-C receptacle J12 VBUS pin (A4) is wired to the red global label 'VBUS' on the same conductor that the blue '+5V' power symbol also drives. On power.kicad_sch (page 7) '+5V' is the mux input IN2 (U5 pin 2) and 'VBUS' is the mux output OUT (U5 pin 1); the two are meant to be separate nets. As drawn, J12.A4 ties '+5V' and 'VBUS' together, shorting the mux input to its own output.",
      "expected": "Spec section 3: 'J12 ... VBUS pins (A4/A9/B4/B9) → +5V net → U5 pin 2/2_1 (IN2)' and 'U5 ... outputs a single OUT ... onto the VBUS net ... distinct from the USB +5V net upstream of the mux.' J12.A4 should be on the +5V net only (mux IN2); the VBUS net (mux OUT / pre-buck rail) must remain separate so the TPS2121 can arbitrate the two supplies.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "mcu.kicad_sch (page 3): J12 pin A4 carries the global label 'VBUS' on the same node as the '+5V' power symbol (junction at the top-left of the USB-C receptacle)."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "J12 (USB_C_Receptacle_USB2.0_14P) VBUS pins (A4/A9/B4/B9) → +5V net → U5 pin 2/2_1 (IN2). ... note this net is named VBUS in the netlist but is distinct from the USB +5V net upstream of the mux."}
      ],
      "impact": "The TPS2121RUXR power mux is bypassed/defeated: its IN2 (+5V) and OUT (VBUS) become the same node, which is also the USB 5 V supply. When the 12 V barrel jack is connected, the mux drives ~12 V onto this node, forcing 12 V onto the USB 5 V rail and back-powering the host port, while the intended seamless 12 V/5 V switchover is lost. The buck (U8) input 'VBUS' is no longer an arbitrated rail.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomaly detected: the USB-C VBUS pin (J12.A4) is tied to the mux-output net 'VBUS' (and shorted to '+5V') instead of to the '+5V' mux-input net, which bypasses the TPS2121 power mux and merges the two input supplies — contradicting the spec's explicit requirement that VBUS and +5V be distinct nets. All other traced interfaces (thermocouple SPI/CS, heater high-side switch, buck regulator, fan TVS clamps, CC pull-downs) match the specification."
}

